<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Danta State</h1><p class="st-meta">1068 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Danta</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Parmar Rajput state in the hills of northern Gujarat whose rulers were hereditary guardians of the Ambaji temple, one of India's major goddess shrines.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parmar-rajputs">Parmar Rajputs</a> claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/paramara-dynasty">Paramara dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>; tradition dates their rule at Danta to 1068. Little is reliably known about the state's early centuries.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Danta was a small, hilly state on the border of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>. Its importance came from the Ambaji temple within its territory, whose management and offerings were controlled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana</a>. Under British rule it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahi-kantha-agency">Mahi Kantha</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banas-kantha-agency">Banas Kantha Agency</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Danta acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947 and merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948; it is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banaskantha-district">Banaskantha district</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. The Ambaji temple remains a major pilgrimage site.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/danta-state.jpg" alt="Danta State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Jaume Ollé · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danta-estat.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1068 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Danta</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Danta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1508&amp;focus=danta-state" aria-label="Danta State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6615 1286 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Danta State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6935 1542L7364 1601M6935 1542L7364 1602M6935 1542L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6935 1542h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6935 1542h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1508&amp;focus=danta-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
